npx prisma db pull // this command use to sync tables from database
npx prisma generate // call after above command

npm install xlsx // to install excel library

npm install mssql // install MsSql library

rm -rf .next        // to delete next build folder
npm run build       // to build next project again

npm cache clean --force
npm cache verify


------------------------------------------------------------------
/_------------- PROJECT CLEAUP -------------_/
/_------------- START -------------_/
1️⃣ Detect unused dependencies (MOST IMPORTANT)
//Install dependency checker
npm install -D depcheck

//Run it
npx depcheck

//Output example
Unused dependencies
➡️ axios
➡️ lodash
➡️ moment
Unused devDependencies
➡️ eslint-plugin-react

2️⃣ Remove unused libraries automatically
//Remove normal dependencies
npm uninstall axios lodash moment

//Remove dev dependencies
npm uninstall eslint-plugin-react --save-dev

3️⃣ Remove orphaned packages (VERY IMPORTANT)

//After uninstalling libraries:
rm -rf node_modules package-lock.json
npm install

This will:
➡️ Cleans unused transitive dependencies
➡️ Fixes corrupted installs
➡️ Reduces node_modules size

4️⃣ Remove unused imports from code (CODE LEVEL CLEANUP)
Option A: ESLint (recommended)

    Add rules:

    "rules": {
    "no-unused-vars": "error",
    "unused-imports/no-unused-imports": "error"
    }

    Install plugin:

    npm install -D eslint-plugin-unused-imports

    Auto-fix:

    npx eslint . --fix

    Option B: TypeScript compiler
    npx tsc --noEmit

    It will show:

    unused imports

    unreachable code

    dead exports

5️⃣ Remove unused scripts & configs

Check & clean:

package.json
"scripts": {
"lint": "...",
"prisma": "...", ❌ remove if unused
"storybook": "..." ❌
}

Remove unused config files

Delete if not used:

.storybook/
jest.config.js
babel.config.js
tailwind.config.js
postcss.config.js
prisma/

6️⃣ Remove unused assets
Images, fonts, videos
npx find-unused-files

Or manually check:

/public/images
/assets

Unused assets increase bundle size.

7️⃣ Analyze bundle (Next.js / React)
Next.js
npm install -D @next/bundle-analyzer

Run:

ANALYZE=true npm run build

This shows:

heavy libraries

unused chunks

8️⃣ Clean build & cache files
rm -rf .next dist build coverage

9️⃣ Final verification
npm run build
npm run lint
npm start

If all pass → project is clean ✅

🔥 Advanced: One-Command Cleanup Script
npx depcheck && \
npm prune && \
rm -rf node_modules package-lock.json && \
npm install

📌 What NOT to remove blindly

❌ next
❌ react / react-dom
❌ eslint / typescript
❌ tailwindcss (if used via classes)
❌ postcss / autoprefixer
❌ dotenv

(depcheck may list them — verify manually)

✅ Final Checklist

✔ Unused dependencies removed
✔ node_modules rebuilt
✔ Unused imports removed
✔ Config files cleaned
✔ Build successful

